```javascript
const SAFE_BASE_DIR = path.resolve(__dirname, 'src');
const safePath = path.join(SAFE_BASE_DIR, pathName);

if (!safePath.startsWith(SAFE_BASE_DIR)) {
  res.writeHead(400, {"Content-Type": "text/plain"});
  res.end("无效的请求路径");
  return;
}
```

This code ensures that any path provided by the user is checked against a safe base directory (`SAFE_BASE_DIR`). If the resolved path does not start with this base directory, the request is considered invalid, and an error message ("无效的请求路径") is returned. This mitigation prevents path traversal attacks by restricting file access to a specific directory. No limitations or side effects are explicitly mentioned in the context.

